import json
from pathlib import Path
D=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
s=json.loads((D/'source.json').read_text())
supported={'q-215768','q-237224','q-237225','q-237036'}
cases=[];ledger=[]
for q in s['record'][':knowledge-point/questions']:
 mid=q[':question/math-academy-id'];level=q.get(':question/difficulty',{}).get(':db/ident','unrated').split('/')[-1]
 f=q.get(':question/answer-fields',[{}])[0];ft=f.get(':answer-field/type',{}).get(':db/ident','missing').split('/')[-1]
 reason=None if mid in supported else ('Referenced AB diagram/coordinates absent from the captured prompt' if mid=='q-167797' else 'Unrated and incomplete answer/solution evidence' if level=='unrated' else 'Radio source bank preserved; numerical option patterns have unresolved generalized recipes. This family is explicitly excluded from generation.')
 cases.append({'source':mid,'database_id':q[':db/id'],'difficulty':level,'field_key':f.get(':answer-field/key'),'field_type':ft,'template':mid,'plot_rating':'moderate (required diagram missing)' if mid=='q-167797' else 'none','supported':mid in supported,'reason':reason,'problem':q[':question/problem'],'solution':q.get(':question/worked-solution'),'correct':f.get(':answer-field/correct',{}).get(':answer/value')})
 for a in f.get(':answer-field/choices',[]):
  ledger.append({'source':mid,'field':f[':answer-field/key'],'answer_uuid':a[':answer/id'],'exact_value':a[':answer/value'],'source_parameters':'All coordinates retained in source.json and classification.json','bank_profile':None if ft=='blank' else mid+'-observed-bank','recipe':'Computed exact RHS -dx/dy*x + Py + (dx/dy)*Px' if mid in supported else 'Retained observed expression only; no generalized recipe claimed','interpretation':'blank canonical answer' if ft=='blank' else 'unresolved; excluded source profile','correct':a[':answer/id']==f.get(':answer-field/correct',{}).get(':answer/id'),'supported':mid in supported})
(D/'classification.json').write_text(json.dumps({'basis':s['basis'],'lineage':s['lineage'],'source_count':len(cases),'cases':cases},indent=2)+'\n')
(D/'choice-ledger.json').write_text(json.dumps(ledger,indent=2)+'\n')
(D/'classification.md').write_text('''# Classification: perpendicular line through a point

Captured math basis 1966, lineage 01a12a15-3e0a-75a1-9dac-f8b8c5d5c3f1. All 12 source practice records and the canonical example are preserved in source.json; classification.json assigns every practice question to a template and field type. The native initial inventory requests classification, not a rated shortage. No generator was registered at this basis.

Easy: six rated records: four RHS blanks (one needs an unavailable diagram) and one text radio? The exact count is five easy records: q-167797, q-215768, q-23453, q-237224, q-237225. The supported text blanks use target x=0, exact integer point differences and rational negative reciprocals. Three observed display layouts are retained separately: q-215768 shows subtraction simplification and an unreduced difference fraction; q-237224 and q-237225 omit the difference fraction and have different signed-coordinate patterns. All three have one field-1 blank expecting the RHS only, no distractor profile, and plot rating none.

Moderate: five rated records: q-103440, q-103455, q-237036, q-72567, q-72568. Four are five-choice equation radios, each assigned its own observed complete-bank profile. q-237036 is the supported field-1 RHS blank; a nonzero target x adds distribution and intercept calculation. Its source has cancellation to zero intercept. The bounded extension permits nonzero and fractional intercepts using the same stages; fractional slopes are evidenced by rated moderate radio prompts, not invented difficulty ratings. Plots: none.

Unrated: q-214038 is an incomplete RHS blank; q-22642 has a five-choice equation bank but no correct reference, difficulty or solution. Neither contributes inventory. Easy diagram family q-167797 references AB without coordinates or an attached plot in the snapshot; it is excluded rather than reconstructing missing visual information from the solution. Its needed plot is moderate, not none.

Every radio option is retained in choice-ledger.json with its field and bank profile. The source has numerically heterogeneous distractors that do not justify complete generalized error recipes. All six observed radio banks (including unrated q-22642) are excluded from generator support. This is a bounded family exception, not a claim of radio replay fidelity. Their original complete, mathematically valid rated questions may still count as inventory if unseen and unreserved.

Hard: unobserved, explicitly examined. The available material teaches two point differences, one negative reciprocal and point-slope simplification. Larger coordinates or extra reduction steps alone do not establish a calibrated hard family. Axis-parallel special cases need a different response shape and are absent from this evidence. The present generator therefore declines hard rather than inflating arithmetic or assigning arbitrary ratings. A hard-rated source, a justified instructional extension and native grading validation reopen this capability decision. Hard remains an explicit unmet five-question band, not filled.
'''.replace('Easy: six rated records: four RHS blanks (one needs an unavailable diagram) and one text radio? The exact count is five easy records:', 'Easy: five rated records: four RHS blanks (one needs an unavailable diagram) and one text radio:'))
(D/'template-extraction.md').write_text('''# Extracted RHS blank families

Source-specific descriptions, original coordinate roles, exact answers and worked solutions are in classification.json; original typed records are in source.json. The four supported banks are q-215768, q-237224, q-237225 and q-237036; each has exactly one canonical RHS math value and no distractors. No mixed fields occur.

Shared move: from reference points A=(a,b), B=(c,d), compute r=(d-b)/(c-a), then m=-1/r. Through P=(h,k), use y-k=m(x-h), distribute and obtain y=mx+(k-mh). Field-1 expects only mx+(k-mh), with y= supplied by the prompt. The canonical example e-14363 supports the method but is not practice inventory.

Fixed components: source wording outside displays, point-slope identities, field key, blank type and RHS notation. Variable components: three integer coordinate pairs, signed subtractions, exact reduced slopes and intercepts. Optional source-layout components: sign simplification and unreduced numerical fractions; q-237036 retains its extra simplified parenthesis before distribution. Every generated variant has one fixed worked solution.

All original coordinate triples are extracted from prompts, not solutions. Sampler bounds [-8,8] include every supported observed value. Easy has h=0; moderate has h!=0 and includes both signs, with the same translated point-slope stages. Both signs and zero y-coordinate are tested. Reference dx!=0 and dy!=0 prevent undefined or axis-parallel slope response shapes. Exact SymPy rationals determine every component. Coordinate sampling is a labeled bounded extension; difficulty uses the observed target-position distinction. Fractional moderate slopes are a cross-field extension supported by the rated radio sources' prompt method.

Replay compares all four supported source answer banks mathematically and correct designation, with exact prompt and prose checks, independently checking every numerical solution row. Display spacing and rational sign normalization are reported separately. Excluded radios retain all original values and source-owned identities in the choice ledger; none has an inferred recipe presented as observed. Unsupported diagram/incomplete families do not enter output.

Question identity hashes rendered problem, solution, answer and difficulty. Mathematical deduplication is stricter: only the exact reduced resulting slope and intercept matter. Translating A and B, changing their separation, changing the target along an unchanged answer line, choosing another source layout, changing seed or IDs cannot add another available task. All source lines (including incomplete prompts) and the canonical line are excluded when preparing new questions.
''')
